Early morning in early spring. On a very narrow rock ledge at the edge of a cliff, high above a misty valley, a small careful tower of plain unpainted wooden toy blocks stands, stacked one by one, the top block set slightly offset as if someone is still placing it with great care. A few spare blocks wait on the ledge, and there is barely any room left on it. Sparse budding shrubs cling to the rock, cold clear air, pale sunrise light from the side, soft haze in the valley below. Tense but calm, quiet focus, a held breath. Medium-wide composition, no person.
